(Test append each from a list variable - plan 250 D1: the parser used to
 read `from source to dest` as a range and swallow the destination)

(Test 1: Append each element from a list held in a variable)
a list called "source" is [10, 20, 30].
a list called "dest" is [].
append each x from source to dest.
print "After append each from list variable:".
print dest's length.
For each n in dest,
  print the n.

(Test 2: The range source form must keep working - it is why D1 was
 ambiguous rather than merely missing)
a list called "rl" is [].
append each n from 1 to 5 to rl.
print "After append each from range:".
print rl's length.
For each n in rl,
  print the n.
